@@ -59,6 +59,22 @@ Each smell reads *what it is* → *how to fix*; match it against the diff:
 
 Issue both sub-agent calls together, in the foreground, and aggregate the reports they return.
 
+**Models.** Spawn the **Standards** sub-agent with `model: sonnet`: it matches the diff against written rules. Spawn the **Spec** sub-agent with `model: sonnet` only when the caller's arguments say `low-risk`; otherwise leave `model` unset so it runs on the session's model, since a missed requirement costs more than the tokens (spay2 grill 2026-11-16 R1-Q6: opus review sub-agents were 53M of 67M weighted tokens in worker sessions).
+
+**Commit trailers.** Add to both the Standards and the Spec brief: "Skip commit trailers such as `Co-Authored-By`: they name the calling session's model, not yours, and the repo's own checks cover them." (spay2 retro 1e05a1e4#3: a sonnet Standards sub-agent flagged `Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus` as the wrong attribution; spay2 retro 94e9ac01#1: a sonnet Spec sub-agent reported the correct `Claude Opus 5.5` trailer as P3.)
+
+**Tool evidence.** Add to both briefs: "A finding that rests on a search or command quotes that command and pastes its output verbatim (the matching lines, or `exit 1, no output`), never a summary of it; with no tool run, say so and drop the claim." (spay2 retro 94e9ac01#2: a Standards sub-agent that said it ran no tools claimed a grep hit that exits 1; #656: one quoted its grep and summarised the output as "the test files did not match" when the output held `tests/pilot-land.test.mjs:205`.)
+
+**Line evidence.** Add to both briefs, next to the tool-evidence sentence: "Each finding at P2 or above, and each hard violation, cites the code line that supports it as `path:line` plus that line's text. Before asserting how code outside the diff behaves, read that line." (ron-skills retro #531-1: a Standards sub-agent that read only the diff reported a P2 that checkpoint targets carry no `worktree`; the caller's loop gives them one.)
+
+**Test results.** Add to both briefs the test commands the caller ran and their exit codes, and: "Review the diff only; rerun no test — the caller already ran these. With no test results given, you may run one single test file." (spay2 retro 00588b5c#1: a Spec sub-agent reran three test files the worker had already passed, hit the 110–120 s tool limit twice in 390 s, and reported no result.)
+
+**Evidence reruns.** Add to the Spec brief: "Changes to an evidence JSON's `sourceVersion`, counts, or `inputs` made by `rerun-evidence.mjs --apply` are expected; do not report them as scope creep." (spay2 retro cdff9918#3: a Spec sub-agent flagged a rerun's count update 1014→1016 as scope creep.)
+
+**Parsed tool output.** Add to the Spec brief: "A finding against code that parses a tool's output must be reproduced with that tool's real output on this machine: paste the command and its output. A finding built on a sample you wrote yourself is marked as a guess and rated no higher than P3." (spay2 retro c3b3a383#2: a Spec sub-agent derived a P2 "the parent suite is listed as failed" from its own synthetic output; real Node v24.21 output of `node scripts/node-test-guarded.mjs` with nested failures lists only the two child tests, so fixing it would have added an unneeded filter.)
+
+**Adapter entries.** When the repo has `scripts/adapter-line.mjs`, add to both briefs: "In `docs/agents/**`, a bare `[Entry]` not followed by `(` or `:` is an adapter entry name that `node scripts/adapter-line.mjs '<Entry>'` resolves; the repo's checks cover it, so do not report it as a broken link." Without `scripts/adapter-line.mjs`, leave this sentence out. (spay2 retro 9580d1e4#1: a Spec sub-agent reported `[Drift check]` in `docs/agents/issue-run-reference.md` as a P2 broken reference link; it is an adapter entry that `adapter-line.mjs "Drift check"` resolves.)
+
 **Standards sub-agent prompt** should include:
 
 - The full diff command and commit list.
